Pages = {820-843},
Month = {SUM},
Abstract = {Barcelona Provincial Council contributes to the design, planning and
   management of healthier cities through the work of the cross-sectoral
   group Urban Environment and Health. This article highlights the
   contributions of two services: Urban Planning (GSHUA), which supports
   municipalities in integrating health criteria into planning, such as
   Vic's POUM (province of Barcelona), awarded the National Urbanism Prize,
   and Public Space and Facilities (GSEIUPA), which promotes healthy public
   spaces. Both have developed innovative, evidence-based tools: a web
   platform to assess health determinants in urban plans, and another to
   evaluate public space interventions. Additionally, resources such as the
   Healthy Streets Guide, tree and urban gardening manuals, and outreach
   activities like the Igualada Urban Green Fair (province of Barcelona),
   help promote healthier environments.},
